.Dd 2026-11-08
.Dt LBTS-FIELDS 5
.\" Manual page created by:
.\" Guus Sliepen <guus@lightbts.info>
.Sh NAME
.Nm lbts fields
.Nd the fields of tickets in LightBTS
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Each ticket has a title, and values for the fields that are defined in the configuration file
.Pa .lightbts/config .
Fields are changed by pseudo-headers at the start of messages, like
.Ql Severity: minor ,
by the commands of
.Xr lbts 1 ,
and by email headers like
.Ql X-LightBTS-Severity .
.Pp
Each field is defined in a section named
.Ql field. Ns Ar name ,
for example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[field.priority]
	type = enum
	values = low, normal, high, urgent
	default = normal
	ordered = true
.Ed
.Pp
These sections can be changed with
.Nm lbts config ,
for example
.Ql lbts config field.priority.default high .
.Xr lbts-init 1
writes the default fields into the configuration of a new instance.
If the configuration has no field sections at all,
as is the case for instances created by older versions of LightBTS,
the default fields are used.
.Pp
When the field definitions are invalid, all commands except
.Nm lbts config
fail with an error that explains the problem.
When they change, the index is rebuilt automatically from the messages,
since the definitions determine which values are valid.
.Sh VARIABLES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va type
The type of the field, see
.Sx TYPES .
Required.
.It Va values
For
.Ql enum
and
.Ql set
fields, the allowed values, separated by commas.
This is optional for
.Ql set
fields; without it, any value is allowed.
.It Va default
The value that new tickets start with, and that a field returns to when it is unset.
For
.Ql set
fields, this can be several values.
.It Va ordered
For
.Ql enum
fields, whether the values are listed in a meaningful order,
so they can be compared in selectors like
.Ql priority>=high .
.It Va min , Va max , Va unit
For
.Ql number
fields, the smallest and largest allowed value,
and a unit that is shown after the value, and may be written after it.
.It Va aliases
Other names for the field in pseudo-headers and selectors, separated by commas.
.It Va label
The name of the field shown by
.Nm lbts show
and the web interface, if it should differ from the name.
.El
.Pp
Other variables are not allowed.
Names of fields and aliases consist of letters, digits,
.Ql -
and
.Ql _ .
Values of
.Ql enum
and
.Ql set
fields can't contain spaces, commas or any of
.Ql = < > ! ,
and can't start with
.Ql +
or
.Ql - .
Names and these values are case-insensitive.
.Sh TYPES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm text
A line of text.
.It Cm enum
One value out of a fixed list.
.It Cm set
Any number of values, optionally out of a fixed list.
.It Cm user
An email address, possibly with a name.
.It Cm date
A date of the form YYYY-MM-DD.
.It Cm number
An integer.
.El
.Sh THE STATUS FIELD
The
.Ql status
field is required, and must be an
.Ql enum
field.
Each status belongs to one of three categories:
.Ql to-do
for work that has not started yet,
.Ql in-progress
for work that has started, and
.Ql done
for work that is finished.
Tickets in the
.Ql done
category are closed, all others are open.
The status field has these extra variables:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va in-progress , Va done
The values in these categories, separated by commas.
All other values are in the
.Ql to-do
category.
.Va done
is required.
.It Va close , Va reopen
The values that
.Nm lbts close
and
.Nm lbts reopen
set.
By default, the first value of
.Va done ,
and the default value.
.El
.Pp
Without a
.Va default ,
the first value that is not done is the default.
.Sh DEFAULT FIELDS
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[field.status]
	type = enum
	values = open, closed
	default = open
	done = closed
	close = closed
	reopen = open

[field.severity]
	type = enum
	values = wishlist, minor, normal, important, serious, critical, grave
	default = normal
	ordered = true

[field.tags]
	type = set
	aliases = tag

[field.owner]
	type = user

[field.milestone]
	type = text

[field.deadline]
	type = date

[field.progress]
	type = number
	min = 0
	max = 100
	unit = %
.Ed
.Sh PSEUDO-HEADERS
A pseudo-header whose name is the name or an alias of a field changes that field.
For fields with a single value,
.Ql -
unsets the field:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
Priority: high
Owner: -
.Ed
.Pp
For
.Ql set
fields,
.Ql + Ns Ar value
or just the value adds it,
.Ql - Ns Ar value
removes it, and
.Ql = Ns Ar value
replaces all values.
A
.Ql + ,
.Ql -
or
.Ql =
on its own applies to the values that follow:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
Tags: patch -moreinfo
Tags: = confirmed security
.Ed
.Pp
Invalid values are reported as warnings, and the rest of the message is still recorded.
The pseudo-headers
.Ql Title ,
.Ql Topic ,
.Ql Description ,
.Ql Version ,
.Ql Found ,
.Ql Notfound ,
.Ql Fixed ,
.Ql Notfixed
and those of the link types are built in,
and their names can't be used for fields.
Neither can
.Ql received
and
.Ql control ,
which LightBTS uses in its own X-LightBTS headers, nor the words
.Ql all ,
.Ql open ,
.Ql closed ,
.Ql to-do ,
.Ql in-progress ,
.Ql done ,
.Ql bugs
and
.Ql tickets ,
which have a meaning in selectors.
.Sh SELECTORS
.Nm lbts list
and the web interface select tickets with these selectors:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm open , closed , all
Tickets whose status is open, closed, or any.
Without any of these, only open tickets are selected.
.It Cm to-do , in-progress , done
Tickets whose status is in the given category.
.It Ar field Ns Cm = Ns Ar value , Ar field Ns Cm != Ns Ar value
Tickets that have, or don't have, the given value.
.It Ar field Ns Cm < Ns Ar value , and likewise Cm <= , > , >=
For ordered
.Ql enum ,
.Ql number
and
.Ql date
fields, tickets whose value compares this way.
.It Ar type Ns Cm = Ns Ar id
Tickets that have a link of the given type to the ticket
.Ar id ,
like
.Ql blocks=12 .
Since a ticket depends on the tickets that block it,
this also selects the tickets that ticket 12 depends on.
.It Ar value
A value of an
.Ql enum
field, or else of a
.Ql set
field with a list of values, or else of any
.Ql set
field, such as a tag.
.El
.Pp
Selecting a status, for example with
.Ql status=wontfix ,
selects tickets in any category, unless a category is given as well.
Conditions with
.Ql =
on the same field match if any of them matches, all other selectors must all match.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr lbts 1 ,
.Xr lbts-web 1 ,
.Xr lightbts 7 .
